  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Build &amp; Design"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Refreshed design, improved ergonomics"
  },
  {
   "t": "h3",
   "html": "A Detector That Evolves With You"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "One of the standout features of the minelab Vanquish 60 detectors is its coil compatibility with Equinox and Coiltek coils."
  },
  {
   "t": "figure",
   "html": "<img src=\"@img:images/60-coils.jpg\" alt=\"whats coils can you use on a new minelab vanquish\" title=\"minelab vanquish 60 series search coils\" width=\"261\" height=\"261\">"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "This is a first for the Vanquish line, and it opens up a world of flexibility. Detectorists can now experiment with different coil sizes and shapes depending on their site and targets—all without upgrading to a new detector. That means greater depth, better separation, or even better handling in iron-rich fields and beaches, just by swapping a coil. It won’t suit everyone, but some people will get more variation and options without having to spend on a more expensive machine. And, if you have one of the Vanquish 60 detectors, you can buy some coils, and then later upgrade to XTERRA or Equinox detector then you already have some accessories."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Minelab Vanquish 560<img src=\"@img:images/60-pc.jpg\" alt=\"where to buy a new minelab vanquish 560\" title=\"when is the new minelab vanquish out to buy\" width=\"261\" height=\"261\">"
